# EQLS Lockouts — redacted fixture, built by analysis/make-fixture.js
#
# Verbatim excerpts from the owner's own EverQuest Legends logs. Every line
# below is exactly as the client wrote it. Nothing has been rewritten: lines
# carrying private conversation were DROPPED WHOLE, because a rewritten line
# still parses into a fake event.
#
# Character: Avenrae, server rivervale. Dropped: 164 private, 30662 unmodelled.
#
# CLOCK: stamps are the game client's local wall clock and carry no timezone.
# The machine that wrote them is set to "Eastern Standard Time"
# (Windows tz id; UTC-05:00 base, DST active in August, so UTC-04:00 for
# these lines). Read off the OS on 21 Aug 2026, not asked for and not guessed.
# Recorded here because every published candidate reset rule is stated in
# Pacific, and without this the comparison is off by an unknown constant.
#
# ENCODING: measured, not assumed. Across all 15 logs, exactly 9 bytes are
# >= 0x80, and all 9 are EF BF BD (U+FFFD). Valid UTF-8. Read as UTF-8.
# The corpus byte total is NOT quoted here: an earlier revision typed
# 440,214,858 into this generated artifact and the measured sum is
# 433,914,867. A figure typed into a file whose whole point is that it is
# generated is the fault this project exists to catch. See analysis/findings.json.
#
# LINE ENDINGS: the source logs are CRLF. This fixture is written LF and
# .gitattributes keeps it that way; the parser strips a trailing CR either way.
#
# Lines beginning with # are this header and are not log content.

